yet are not blank (Note); the missing `$` anchor (Note); a plant red on the pin's own old rows as well (Note: the builder disclosed p7, p7b, p11); a limit of the key-list pin (px2c: Note); the parser dropping the whole register for an old invisible-only entry (Note, plain words); the commit-3 message figures; the PR body's builder-sourced figures; the unsigned head; the title length; CodeQL neutral explained, or CI/CodeQL PENDING at the verdict (Condition); local fonts vs the runner; Node 26 (builder) vs Node 24 (CI) (Note). Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the plant, the row and the number.** **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs C1-C9 measured with their controls, zero findings above Note, every `Analyze (<language>)` complete at `2eec1997` (or on the merge ref) with open alerts zero (control fired), `CodeQL` concluded and explained, the five required contexts `success`; GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only (an open item named on the line above the last line); **NO GO on any Blocker or Major = NO GO round 1 of 2 on this class**, with the fix-shape in prose (round 2 is a fix kit; not the cap). A security-shaped finding you cannot classify is a STOP: say it is tier-1 and unresolved.
